= Ernst Meyer

A Spartacist of the first hour, a journalist from East Prussia with a weak chest and a steady temper. [? if march_action = 1 : After the defeat of March 1921, the party turned to him to put the pieces back together. ?][? if march_action != 1 : He is the man the party sends for when the currents stop speaking to each other. ?]

- @consolidate
- @centre
- @root: Return to main

@consolidate
title: Rebuild the Organisation
subtitle: Patient work in every district. The party's spine strengthens.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer = 1 : Next advisor action in 1 month. ?][? if advisor_action_timer > 1 : Next advisor action in [+ advisor_action_timer +] months. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.advisor_action_timer = 4;
Q.last_advisor_action = 1;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] += 4;
}
Q.unity += 5;
Q.militancy -= 2;
!}

Meyer visits the districts one by one, reopens the offices that were closed and pays the printers who were not paid. Nobody cheers. The party works again.

@centre
title: Steer Between Left and Right
subtitle: Give both wings something. Each suspects the other got more.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer = 1 : Next advisor action in 1 month. ?][? if advisor_action_timer > 1 : Next advisor action in [+ advisor_action_timer +] months. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 4; last_advisor_action = 1; offensive_satisfaction += 6; unionist_satisfaction += 6; luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 2; unity += 2

Meyer writes a resolution that both Ruth Fischer and Heinrich Brandler can vote for. It says very little, very carefully.
